A :CASE branch whose only :RETURN sits inside an :IF can fall through when
the condition is false, so it still needs an :EXITCASE: prefer_exitcase
fires on that :CASE (issue #139 final-statement-only rule;
diag.prefer_exitcase last Flags fence).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE FirstMatch;
	:PARAMETERS nKind, bStrict;
	:BEGINCASE;
	:CASE nKind == 1;
		:IF bStrict;
			:RETURN "strict";
		:ENDIF;
	:OTHERWISE;
		:EXITCASE;
	:ENDCASE;
	:RETURN "loose";
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE FirstMatch;
	:PARAMETERS nKind, bStrict;
	:BEGINCASE;
	:CASE nKind == 1;
		:IF bStrict;
			:RETURN "strict";
		:ENDIF;
	:OTHERWISE;
		:EXITCASE;
	:ENDCASE;
	:RETURN "loose";
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:2-4:7 warning prefer_exitcase: ':CASE' block should end with ':EXITCASE;'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:2-4:7 warning prefer_exitcase: ':CASE' block should end with ':EXITCASE;'
